<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Cape Colony</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1652</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Cape Colony was the settlement at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cape-of-good-hope">Cape of Good Hope</a> established in 1652 by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch-east-india-company">Dutch East India Company</a> as a resupply station for ships sailing to Asia. It grew into a settler colony whose descendants formed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/afrikaners">Afrikaner</a> community. The colony was a lasting legacy of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch-empire">Dutch Empire</a> and passed to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> in the early nineteenth century.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/cape-colony.jpg" alt="Cape Colony" width="320" height="160" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Sodacan · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_Cape_Colony_(1876%E2%80%931910).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
